{
  "tree_id": 1167,
  "family": "Rosaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Prunus ilicifolia ssp. lyonii &lt;/em&gt;is a subspecies of Hollyleaf Cherry. A multi-stemmed shrub to small tree, this species naturally forms a rounded shape with dense, unkempt branching. Its shiny, dark green leaves are slightly variable in form, yet distinctive from those of &lt;em&gt;Prunus ilicifolia ssp. ilicifolia&lt;/em&gt; by being  broad, less stiff, and lacking serrate margins. Its small, cream-colored flowers bloom on showy upright clusters. The following black drupes resemble small cherries and are a favorite food for local birds and bats. This drought-tolerant species is adapted to dry summer conditions and is relatively fast-growing. However, its fallen fruits can stain concrete.&nbsp;",
